    "id": "q02",
    "question": "At which temperature and voltage is the pinch stop time worst, according to our lessons learned?",
    "answer": {
      "found": true,
      "answer": "According to LL-2022-02, the worst case for pinch stop time is cold and low supply voltage together: -30 °C and 9 V. On the WLC-100, the stop time there was 12 to 15 ms against a 10 ms limit, versus 5 to 7 ms at 23 °C. The lesson is to test that corner on every software release.",
